{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And He closed up flesh in its place.</b> They said in the Midrash (Genesis Rabbah 17:6) that the letter סמ״ך is not found in the Torah until the woman was created, because the Satan was created with her. And one may give a reason why specifically סמ״ך more than ט״ת or נ״ן — because סמ״ך is an expression of סמיכה, leaning, to indicate that on account of the woman a person needs סמיכה, for HaShem supports his hand so that he does not fall into her snare, as it is written (Proverbs 19:14), ״וּמֵה׳ אִשָּׁה מַשְׂכָּלֶת״, and He supports his hand also so that he does not fall into the hands of his evil inclination, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Kiddushin 30b): were it not that the Holy One, blessed be He, helps him, he could not prevail against it. And this סמיכה is alluded to in the verse ״וַיִּסְגֹּר בָּשָׂר תַּחְתֶּנָּה״ — that the Holy One, blessed be He, closes on his behalf so that he not stumble through her, in the language of ״וַיִּסְגֹּר ה׳ בַּעֲדוֹ,״ which is a closing of shelter. And what is written, ״וַיִּבֶן ה׳ אֶת הַצֵּלָע״ — the expression of building is mentioned to indicate that in this joining there is need only for the purpose that the world be built and not destroyed, as it is written (Genesis 30:3), ״וְאִבָּנֶה גַּם אָנֹכִי מִמֶּנָּה,״ for through children a person is called built, and likewise בן is derived from the expression of building, as Rashi explained (Genesis 5:28) on the verse ״וַיּוֹלֶד בֵּן.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:26:53.739018223Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}